  2	 * WP-009 QA: Server-level routing tests for the 5 knowledge HTTP endpoints.
  3	 *
  4	 * These tests exercise the HTTP dispatch layer in gui/server.ts — specifically
  5	 * that each route is correctly wired, that query-string parameters are parsed
  6	 * and forwarded to the handler, that the two body-parsing routes (PATCH and
  7	 * POST /move) use handleRequest() special-case branches, and that the three
  8	 * body-free routes (GET, DELETE, POST /promote) are dispatched through
  9	 * matchRoute().
 10	 *
 11	 * AC coverage:
 12	 *   AC-1  GET /api/knowledge — routes through matchRoute(), all query params parsed
 13	 *   AC-2  DELETE /api/knowledge/:id — routes through matchRoute(), scope/project_slug from QS
 14	 *   AC-3  POST /api/knowledge/:id/promote — routes through matchRoute(), scope/project_slug from QS
 15	 *   AC-4  PATCH /api/knowledge/:id — special case in handleRequest(), body parsing + error handling
 16	 *   AC-5  POST /api/knowledge/:id/move — special case in handleRequest(), body parsing + error handling
 17	 *   AC-6  Two-tier dispatch pattern (body-free in matchRoute, body-parsing in handleRequest)
 18	 *   AC-7  Knowledge routes do not interfere with existing routes (insights, projects, orchestrator)
 19	 *
 20	 * Edge cases:
 21	 *   - PATCH with oversized body returns 413
 22	 *   - POST /move with oversized body returns 413
 23	 *   - PATCH with invalid JSON body returns 400
 24	 *   - POST /move with invalid JSON body returns 400
 25	 *   - GET /api/knowledge with no query params returns 200 JSON array (empty store)
 26	 *   - DELETE /api/knowledge/:id without scope returns 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
 27	 *   - POST /api/knowledge/:id/promote with scope=global returns 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
